\caption{Task scale and analytic localization sensitivity. (a) All converted-label VisDrone validation ground truth (548 images, 38,759 boxes), after the independent-axis resizing to $640\times640$ used by the common evaluator. The equivalent side is $s=\sqrt{w_{\rm in}h_{\rm in}}$; all five bins and their rounded proportions are shown. These input-scale bins differ from the original-image COCO area ranges used for $\mathrm{AP}_{s}$. (b) For equal-size axis-aligned boxes with unchanged vertical position, a horizontal shift gives $\mathrm{IoU}=(w-d)/(w+d)$ for $0\leq d<w$. A one-pixel shift yields 0.778 for $w=8$ and 0.939 for $w=32$. This is an analytic geometry illustration, not a measurement of model localization errors.}
\label{fig:motivation}
\end{figure*}
